n" [:option {:value "9000277"} "15 kilometres (Freestyle), Men"] "\n" [:option {:value "9000278"} "50 kilometres (Mass Start, Classical), Men"] "\n" [:option {:value "9000280"} "4 × 10 kilometres Relay, Men"] "\n" [:option {:value "9000281"} "Team Sprint (Freestyle), Men"] "\n" [:option {:value "9000286"} "Sprint (Classical), Women"] "\n" [:option {:value "9000298"} "10 kilometres (Freestyle), Women"] "\n" [:option {:value "9000299"} "30 kilometres (Mass Start, Classical), Women"] "\n" [:option {:value "9000300"} "15 kilometres Skiathlon, Women"] "\n" [:option {:value "9000301"} "4 × 5 kilometres Relay, Women"] "\n" [:option {:value "9000302"} "Team Sprint (Freestyle), Women"]] [:script {} "$('#same_games_select').change(function(){location.href='/results/' + $('#same_games_select').val();})"]] " | " [:form {:class "form-inline form-inline-header"} [:select {:name "id", :id "other_games_select", :class "form-control"} [:option {:value ""} "In other Games"] "\n" [:option {:value "2131"} "2006"] "\n" [:option {:value "923551"} "2010"] "\n" [:option {:value "350068"} "2014"] "\n" [:option {:value "19019714"} "2022"] "\n" [:option {:value "15000135"} "2026"]] [:script {} "$('#other_games_select').change(function(){location.href='/results/' + $('#other_games_select').val();})"]] " | " [:a {:href "/event_names/190"} "Event type"]] [:h1 {:class "event_title"} "30 kilometres Skiathlon, Men" [:small {}]] [:table {:class "biodata"} [:tbody {} [:tr {} [:th {} "Date"] [:td {} "11 February 2018 — 15:15"]] [:tr {} [:th {} "Status"] [:td {} "Olympic"]] [:tr {} [:th {} "Location"] [:td {} [:a {:href "/venues/937"} "Alpensia Cross-Country Centre, Alpensia Resort, Mountain Cluster, Daegwallyeong"]]] [:tr {} [:th {} "Participants"] [:td {} [:a {:href "/events/9000279"} "68 from 30 countries"]]] [:tr {} [:th {:valign "top"} "Details"] [:td {} "Course Length: 15,484 m / 15,100 m" [:br {}] "Height Differential: 58 m / 41 m" [:br {}] "Maximum Climb: 33 m / 35 m" [:br {}] "Total Climbing: 552 m / 604 m"]]]] [:div {:class "description"} [:p {} "As in the last three Winter Olympics, the 30 km skiathlon event consisted of a 15 km section in the classical technique, followed immediately, after a change of skis, by another 15 km in the freestyle technique. Among the favorites were the Swiss defending champion " [:a {:href "/athletes/118753"} "Dario Cologna"] ", and Norway’s rising star " [:a {:href "/athletes/137724"} "Johannes Høsflot Klæbo"] ". The 2017 world champion, and Tour de Ski winner " [:a {:href "/athletes/128329"} "Sergey Ustyugov"] ", was not allowed to compete by the IOC, due to the finding of the McLaren-Report. In the 2017-18 season, only one men’s skiathlon was contested, at Lillehammer in December 2017 with four Norwegians finishing in the first four: Klæbo first, then triple World Cup winner " [:a {:href "/athletes/118807"} "Martin Johnsrud Sundby"] ", followed by " [:a {:href "/athletes/137722"} "Hans Christer Holund"] " and " [:a {:href "/athletes/137726"} "Simen Hegstad Krüger"] ". Krüger was a relative newcomer, having won his first World Cup race in December 2017, over 15 km freestyle.\nIn PyeongChang, nobody dared to break away from a large leading group for the first 25 km, with the favorites still cautious, and pace moderate. Krüger, less fancied than his compatriots, was involved in a fall, along with two OAR athletes, just a few hundred metres from the start. But with less than 5 km from the finish line, he got into a position where he was in with a chance to escape the pack, and he took it, and within just one kilometer, Krüger opened a gap of 22 seconds. The pursuers hesitated for too long as it was not until about 27 km that Sundby started the pursuit , with Holund close behind. But Krüger held on to his lead to become a surprise winner with Sundby second, just eight seconds behind and Holund in third, another two seconds adrift. Most of the favorites finished among the top ten: " [:a {:href "/athletes/118811"} "Maurice Manificat"] " from France was fifth, Cologna sixth, Canadian " [:a {:href "/athletes/118722"} "Alex Harvey"] " eighth, and Klæbo tenth."] "\n\n" [:p {} "With a clean sweep in the first men’s event, the Norwegians gave an indication of their superiority in the men’s cross-country in PyeongChang. Like other races in the first few days of the Games, it was characterized by ice cold weather of minus 13° C and stormy gusts of wind."] "\n"] [:button {:id "button241859", :class "btn btn-default"} "Details"] [:script {} "$('#button241859').click(splits)"] [:table {:class "table table-striped"} [:thead {} [:tr {} [:th {} "Pos"] [:th {} "Number"] [:th {} "Competitor"] [:th {} "NOC"] [:th {} "Time"] [:th {:style "display: none", :class "split"} "Classical"] [:th {:style "display: none", :class "split"} "Pit Stop"] [:th {:style "display: none", :class "split"} "Freestyle"] [:th {}] [:th {}] [:th {}]]] [:tbody {} [:tr {:class "", :style ""} [:td {} "1"] [:td {:class "bib"} "7"] [:td {} [:a {:href "/athletes/137726"} "Simen Hegstad Krüger"]] [:td {} [:a {:href "/countries/NOR"} [:img {:style "padding-right: 2px; vertical-align: middle", :src "https://olympedia-flags.s3.eu-central-1.amazonaws.com/NOR.png"}] "NOR"]] [:td {} "1-16:20.0"] [:td {:class "split", :style "display: none"} "40:46.1 (14)"] [:td {:class "split", :style "display: none"} "27.7 (8)"] [:td {:class "split", :style "display: none"} "35:06.2 (1)"] [:td {} [:span {:class "Gold"} "Gold"]] [:td {}] [:td {}]] [:tr {:class "", :style ""} [:td {} "2"] [:td {:class "bib"} "6"] [:td {} [:a {:href "/athletes/118807"} "Martin Johnsrud Sundby"]] [:td {} [:a {:href "/countries/NOR"} [:img {:style "padding-right: 2px; vertical-align: middle", :src "https://olympedia-flags.s3.eu-central-1.amazonaws.com/NOR.png"}] "NOR"]] [:td {} "1-16:28.0"] [:td {:class "split", :style "display: none"} "40:30.5 (2)"] [:td {:class "split", :style "display: none"} "35.1 (57)"] [:td {:class "split", :style "display: none"} "35:22.4 (2)"] [:td {} [:sp